msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:123
msgid "Blog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:125
msgid ""
"New releases and deep-dives are written up on the :doc:`blog <blog>`. Blog "
"provides a RSS feed (the icon at the top of the blog page) so you can "
"receive notifications of new blog posts from your reader."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:130
msgid "Other internal optimizations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:132
msgid ""
"Fonts and icons are served directly from this site, not from third-party "
"CDNs such as Google Fonts. This means the docs renders the same from all "
"countries (e.g. mainland China). Each font includes only the glyphs used by "
"the site, keeping page weight small."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:137
msgid "Links to this site shared on social medias show rich preview cards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:139
msgid ""
"Every page declares a canonical URL and is listed in a generated ``sitemap."
"xml``, so search engines can discover and index the whole site."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:142
msgid ""
"The docs build is strict: Python code snippets are syntax-checked, and "
"broken links or unresolved API cross-references make the build fail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:146
msgid "Linking from your own docs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:148
msgid ""
"Other Sphinx projects can cross-reference psutil's API directly through the "
"`intersphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/master/usage/extensions/"
"intersphinx.html>`_ extension. Add psutil to ``intersphinx_mapping`` in your "
"``conf.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:152
msgid ""
"intersphinx_mapping = {\n"
"    \"psutil\": (\"https://psutil.io/\", None),\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:158
msgid ""
"You can then reference any psutil object and it links straight here, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:160
msgid "See :func:`psutil.cpu_times` function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../about.rst:164
msgid ""
"This will automatically turn ``psutil.cpu_times`` into a link pointing to "
"this site."
msgstr ""
